WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.184
The paper makes three main contributions.

00:00:03.264 --> 00:00:06.448
First,

00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:09.712
it introduces a novel formulation of the unbalanced
optimal transport problem that connects

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:12.976
the rigorous theory of semi-couplings,

00:00:13.056 --> 00:00:16.240
which allow mass to vary,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.504
with a practical and scalable optimal-transport
mapping estimator.

00:00:19.584 --> 00:00:22.768
Second,

00:00:22.848 --> 00:00:26.032
it derives a computationally feasible
implementation based on dual potentials parameterized

00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:29.296
by input convex neural networks,

00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:32.560
together with learned reweighting functions that
predict mass changes.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.824
Third,

00:00:35.904 --> 00:00:39.088
it proposes a new cycle-consistent training
procedure that alternates between updating

00:00:39.168 --> 00:00:42.352
these maps and rescaling functions,

00:00:42.432 --> 00:00:45.616
and crucially generalizes to new, out-of-sample cells.

00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:48.880
Together these give the first neural method that
estimates semi-couplings for unbalanced OT at single-cell scale.
